<spell-notebook "step theming">
	<header level="1">
		Step
		<header>A step shows the completion status of an activity in a series of activities.</>
	</>
	<step-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
				<ui-item link="#themes">Themes</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-step-*` and `--ui-steps-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (a region,
			`:root`), or on the group's box through `::part(steps)`. Every step in the group reads them from the group, so set
			them there or above, not on one step.

			- The content's look tokens (`--ui-step-content-padding`, `--ui-step-description-distance` ...) also work on one
			  step.
			- Style one step's box with `ui-step::part(step)`, and its `icon`, `content`, `title` and `description` parts
			  likewise.
			- Never set the `--_ui-step*` names: they're the sheet's private plumbing (the group resolves its variations into
			  them).
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-steps {
			  --ui-step-completed-color: var(--ui-primary);
			  --ui-step-active-background: var(--ui-surface-muted);
			  --ui-step-padding: 1em 1.5em;
			}
			ui-step::part(title) {
			  font-weight: normal;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-step" playground>
				<ui-steps>
					<ui-step icon="truck" heading="Shipping" description="Choose your shipping options"></>
				</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling this component through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
